  "design_notes": "Mossback reads as a low, stout box on two long treads with a fat upright drum on its back and a fringe of green cubes breaking its outline, so even in fog its silhouette is a slow, heavy pack animal. Everything is long, low and continuous: the treads run the full body length with no sharp front or back, the head sits forward and low like a tortoise, and the square spout juts sideways toward the trees on its loop, because this machine is built to keep moving and pour without ever turning to face anything. It has no arms, which is its blind spot made literal: it cannot stop, reach or defend itself, it can only carry and roll on. Weathered teal paint worn through to rust-brown straps and bare metal tells decades of rain, a faded safety-yellow stripe on the tank ties it back to Gridhaven's city order, and the moss green cubes show the Grove slowly claiming it. Soft white oval eyes in a wide low screen give it the tired, kind gaze of an old engine, with small amber tail lights that the camera sees as it rolls away mid-sentence."
}